<Layout title="Plant Identification Disclaimer" description="Important accuracy and safety limitations for automated plant identification from photos." canonicalPath="/disclaimer/">
  <section class="page-hero"><div class="container"><p class="eyebrow">Safety disclaimer</p><h1>A likely match is not a safety verdict.</h1></div></section>
  <section class="section-tight"><div class="container prose"><div class="legal-note"><strong>Plant identification from photos may be incorrect.</strong> Do not rely on this tool alone when deciding whether a plant, berry, mushroom or other material is edible, medicinal, poisonous or safe for pets.</div><h2>Verify high-stakes decisions</h2><p>Consult a qualified local botanist, horticulturist, veterinarian, medical professional or poison control service when safety matters. Do not taste or handle an unknown plant based on a result shown here.</p><h2>Why matches can be wrong</h2><p>Lighting, image quality, plant age, seasonal changes, hybrids and visually similar species can all reduce accuracy. Confidence scores describe model similarity, not a guarantee of identity or safety.</p></div></section>
</Layout>
